# The build context is shipped to the daemon in full on every build, so this
# file is about build time and data hygiene, NOT image size: docker/Dockerfile
# copies only pyproject.toml, the three metadata files and src/, and its
# runtime stage copies nothing but the virtualenv. Without these rules the
# context was 4.3 GB, of which test_data/ alone was 3.4 GB of real screen
# data that has no business being sent anywhere.
*
# Everything the wheel build actually needs, re-admitted by name so a new
# large directory cannot silently rejoin the context.
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES
!src/
src/**/__pycache__/
src/**/*.pyc
